1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Going $500 over a

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,440
line cost Linda

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:06,627
$1,148.

4
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:08,080
That's not a tax

5
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:09,040
bracket.

6
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:10,560
That's a cliff.

7
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:11,680
And this one hides

8
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:14,080
inside your Medicare bill.

9
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,280
Meet Linda.

10
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,600
She's 66,

11
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:17,640
she's retired,

12
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:19,400
and she files single.

13
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,960
In 2024,

14
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:22,800
her roof started leaking.

15
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:23,600
So she pulled an

16
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:25,760
extra $14,000 out of

17
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:26,960
her IRA to fix

18
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:27,800
it.

19
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:29,040
That pushed her income

20
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:30,000
for the year to

21
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,160
$109,500.

22
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,880
And nothing happened.

23
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:35,800
Her taxes went up

24
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:36,440
a little,

25
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:37,120
the way a bucket

26
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,120
should.

27
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:39,120
Then,

28
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:39,840
near the end of

29
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:41,160
2025,

30
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:42,760
a letter showed up.

31
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,280
Starting in January,

32
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:45,440
her Medicare Part B

33
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:46,880
premium would jump from

34
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:47,680
$202.90 to

35
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:53,120
$284.10 a month.

36
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:55,600
Plus $14.50 a month

37
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:56,560
more for her drug

38
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:57,720
plan.

39
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:01,520
That's $1,148 a year.

40
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:02,440
For a roof she

41
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:04,640
fixed two years ago.

42
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:06,320
Linda called Social Security

43
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:07,200
and asked if they'd

44
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,560
made a mistake.

45
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:09,760
They hadn't.

46
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:10,960
The rule is called

47
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,160
IRMAA.

48
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:13,120
Medicare looks at your

49
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:14,320
tax return from two

50
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:15,600
years back.

51
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:17,040
And income here means

52
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:18,680
more than a paycheck.

53
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:20,240
Medicare even adds back

54
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:22,920
tax-free municipal bond interest.

55
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:24,720
Money the IRS doesn't

56
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:25,920
tax can still push

57
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:27,080
you over.

58
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:28,240
It also doesn't work

59
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:29,520
like a bracket.

60
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:31,040
A bracket only taxes

61
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,440
the overflow.

62
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:33,840
IRMAA doesn't care how

63
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:35,440
far over you went.

64
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:36,480
Cross the line by

65
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:37,400
one dollar,

66
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:38,400
and the whole step

67
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,880
lands on you.

68
00:01:40,368 --> 00:01:42,080
It's a cliff.

69
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:43,280
Linda went over by

70
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,880
$500.

71
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:45,760
If she'd gone over

72
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,840
by $28,000,

73
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:49,320
she'd pay exactly the

74
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:50,200
same.

75
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:51,120
And it isn't one

76
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,000
cliff.

77
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,200
It's a staircase,

78
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,920
with five steps.

79
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:56,160
The first step adds

80
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:58,880
$81.20 a month.

81
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,000
The last one adds

82
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,480
$487.

83
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,480
At the top,

84
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:04,920
a single person pays

85
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:08,080
$689.90 a month for

86
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:09,640
Part B alone.

87
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:11,040
For a married couple,

88
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:12,080
the first line sits

89
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:14,800
at $218,000.

90
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:15,600
And both of them

91
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:16,920
pay the step.

92
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,400
So one dollar over

93
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,600
costs a couple about

94
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:22,440
$2,300 a year.

95
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,680
So what could Linda

96
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:24,840
have done?

97
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:25,760
She could have spread

98
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:27,000
it out.

99
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,960
$14,000 in one year

100
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:30,800
went over the cliff.

101
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,480
$7,000 in each of

102
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:33,600
two years would have

103
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,080
stayed in the bucket.

104
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:36,160
The same goes for

105
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:37,680
Roth conversions and big

106
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:39,040
stock sales.

107
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:40,240
Check the line before

108
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:41,080
you do it,

109
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:42,400
not after.

110
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,920
If you're already close,

111
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:45,120
a few hundred dollars

112
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:46,280
matters.

113
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:47,400
Know your number in

114
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:48,000
December,

115
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:48,800
while the year is

116
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,920
still open.

117
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,360
And watch your age.

118
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:52,400
The income you have

119
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:54,160
at 63 sets your

120
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:54,960
premium at

121
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:56,320
65.

122
00:02:56,320 --> 00:02:57,440
There is one way

123
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:58,240
out.

124
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:59,440
If your income dropped

125
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:00,640
because of a life-changing

126
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:01,360
event,

127
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,960
like retiring or losing

128
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,080
a spouse,

129
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,280
you can file form

130
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:08,000
SSA-44 and ask Social

131
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,280
Security to use your

132
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:09,920
newer,

133
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:11,360
lower income.

134
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,480
But a leaky roof

135
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:14,620
